{"meta":{"ticker":"CGDV","as_of_date":"2026-10-19","performance_as_of":"2026-09-30","generated_at":"2026-10-20 08:42:10"},"benchmark":{"ticker":"SPY","fund_name":"State Street SPDR S&P 500 ETF"},"overview":{"ticker":"CGDV","fund_name":"Capital Group Dividend Value ETF","category":"US Large-Cap Value","issuer":"Capital Group","index_name":null,"region":"North America","exchange":"NYSEARCA","expense_ratio":0.0033,"aum":39184270000,"holdings_count":56,"inception_date":"2022-02-22","overall_score":5.8683831043711,"overall_rank":460,"sector_diversification_score":6.40603408940373},"description":{"tsi_description":"CGDV is an actively managed U.S. equity ETF that emphasizes companies with dividend-paying potential alongside strong earnings growth and quality characteristics. The fund uses a multi-manager approach and differs from many traditional dividend or value ETFs by maintaining meaningful exposure to growth-oriented companies with accelerating fundamentals. CGDV has historically shown less concentration in mega-cap technology stocks than the S&P 500 while still maintaining substantial exposure to market leaders. The portfolio emphasizes forward-looking earnings growth and profitability metrics rather than relying strictly on traditional value screens or high dividend yields. Overall, CGDV offers a more growth-oriented interpretation of dividend and value investing than many passive peers.","strategy_steps":["Actively managed by Capital Group using a multi-manager investment approach.","Invests primarily in U.S. equities with dividend-paying characteristics or dividend-paying potential.","Emphasizes companies with attractive long-term earnings growth prospects.","Incorporates forward-looking fundamental analysis in the security selection process.","Maintains exposure to companies with strong profitability and quality characteristics.","Allows investment in both dividend-paying and low-yielding growth-oriented companies.","Constructs the portfolio independently of tra